## Selected matrix-valued source

For the frozen anchor `p=21817`, `gamma=5`, and each canonical basis vector
`k_j` of `K6`, define

```text
S_j = u*v*k_j*(t0*t1*t2)*C_section,  j=1,...,18.
```

Every term has Cox degree `(9,1,2)` and lies in the complete 42,706-row H02
ambient basis.  The assembled source matrix has shape `42706 x 18` and 615
nonzero entries.  No observed value, continuous coefficient or discrete fit
choice enters this construction.

## Exact anchor decision

Solving all 18 columns through the same frozen corrected G3BI endpoint chart
gives zero residual.  The resulting B103 H02 quotient matrix has shape
`248 x 18` and exact rank

```text
rank(S_K6 -> H02_quotient) = 18  over GF(21817).
```

Appending the independently computed G3CA `P_delta` quotient row raises the
rank to 19.  Thus the selected source injection is faithful on `K6`, and the
old scalar `P_delta` direction is not hidden inside its image.

This is a positive source theorem.  UST.G3GI showed that no scalar
catalecticant maps `K6` into the selected inverse-system plane; UST.G3GJ now
shows that the selected Cox/H02 construction does retain all 18 directions.

## Same-field boundary

The archived UST.G3CQ transform-defect coefficients were executed at
`GF(11), gamma=3`, at the B89 proof fiber.  The G3GJ source and G3FR target
anchor are at `GF(21817), gamma=5`, at the corrected endpoint.  Those finite
coordinate tables cannot be composed merely because the abstract sequence
of operations is the same.

The next theorem must therefore do one of the following:

1. execute Jacobian division, original-partial correction, minus divergence
   and H02 normal projection directly at `(21817,5)` on all 18 columns; or
2. prove a hash-bound base-change/naturality intertwiner carrying the G3CQ
   operator to that endpoint.

Only the resulting same-field `136 x 18` plane map may be compared with the
G3FR primitive-15 target.  Equality at the anchor would still require replay
on the other 47 fibers before any `Q(gamma)` promotion.

